---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="How we compare plans" description={`How ${SITE_NAME} ranks and compares phone plans, and what each detail means.`}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1 class="display">How we compare plans</h1>
    <h2>Prices</h2>
    <p>Prices are for one line per month, with autopay where the carrier offers a discount for it, before taxes and fees. Some MVNOs only reach their lowest price when you pay for several months upfront; we say so on the plan.</p>
    <h2>What the details mean</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>Premium data</dt><dd>High-priority data. When a tower is busy, carriers slow down lower-priority users first. After you use your premium data, you can still use data, but it may slow down at busy times.</dd>
      <dt>Hotspot</dt><dd>How much high-speed data you can share with a laptop or tablet. Some plans allow unlimited hotspot at a reduced speed.</dd>
      <dt>Network</dt><dd>The towers your phone uses. MVNOs and prepaid brands use one of the big three networks, so coverage is usually the same as that carrier's.</dd>
    </dl>
    <h2>How the finder ranks plans</h2>
    <p>Every plan starts with a score based on price. Your answers then add points: lower prices when price matters most, plans from the big three when coverage matters most, included streaming when perks matter most, more premium data for heavy use, and more hotspot data if you use it every day. The “why it fits” line lists the reasons that counted most.</p>
    <h2>Best value in a comparison</h2>
    <p>When you compare plans, we mark the lowest price, the most premium data, the most hotspot and the most perks. If every plan is the same in a row, nothing is marked.</p>
    <h2>Keeping it accurate</h2>
    <p>Carriers change plans often. Each plan links to the carrier page it came from and shows when we last checked it. Plans we haven't checked yet are marked “not yet verified”. Always confirm details with the carrier before you switch.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 760px; padding-block: 24px 64px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; font-size: 17px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 48px); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  h2 { font-size: 22px; margin-top: 16px; }
  dl { margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  dt { font-weight: 700; }
  dd { margin: 0; }
</style>
